[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Tesseract OCR Setup on Windows (Phase 3)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFor documents that contain scanned pages or photographs with little or no extractable digital text, the system invokes Tesseract OCR.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 1. Install Tesseract OCR on Windows[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Download the Windows installer (64-bit) from the official UB-Mannheim repository:[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   👉 [https://github.com/UB-Mannheim/tesseract/wiki](https://github.com/UB-Mannheim/tesseract/wiki)[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Run the installer:[m
[32m+[m[32m   - When asked to choose components, expand **"Additional script data"** and check **"Devanagari script"**.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Expand **"Additional language data"** and check **"Marathi"** and **"Hindi"**.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Default install path is `C:\Program Files\Tesseract-OCR`.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. Add Tesseract to your Windows System PATH:[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Open Windows Search -> "Environment Variables" -> Edit `Path` -> Add `C:\Program Files\Tesseract-OCR`.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Alternatively, configure `TESSERACT_CMD=C:\Program Files\Tesseract-OCR\tesseract.exe` in your `.env`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 2. Verify Language Packs[m
[32m+[m[32mIn Windows PowerShell or Git Bash, run:[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mtesseract --list-langs[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m**Expected Output:**[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mList of installed languages (4):[m
[32m+[m[32meng[m
[32m+[m[32mhin[m
[32m+[m[32mmar[m
[32m+[m[32mosd[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32mIf `mar` is missing, download `mar.traineddata` from the [tessdata_fast repository](https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata_fast/raw/main/mar.traineddata) and place it in `C:\Program Files\Tesseract-OCR\tessdata\`.[m
 [m
